INTERPRETATION
Use only the bases whose simulated round-number shares match the real ones. On those,
if the recovery ratios are all below one and close together, the attenuation account
in the paper is supported. If they straddle one, it is not, and the sentence should be
withdrawn rather than defended. Note also that the shipped R reader defines its
residual share as one minus the sum of the non-unit weights, which with weights that
sum to one makes it identically the grain-one weight, so the residual column carries
no information beyond the first row.

